--TEST--
`Core\Task::all` reads each field's type off the `fn` literal written there, so a field holding a `callable` variable, and an argument that is a variable at all, are both refused — `rule:concurrency/all-answers-a-typed-shape`, `rule:types/callable-absorbs-closure`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// § 1: "a field whose value is a `callable`-typed variable rather than a
// literal is a compile error naming the field, because there is nothing to
// bind from". `rule:types/closure-literal` leaves `callable` without a signature, so `$loader`
// carries no record of what it returns — the type exists only at the literal.
//
// The two refusals are one rule at two widths. A field that is not a literal
// loses that field; an *argument* that is not a literal loses every field at
// once, which is why it is refused as a whole rather than field by field.
// `rule:types/grammar`'s deferred typed-`callable` signatures are what would lift
// both, and that ADR's *Revisiting* is where the case is counted.
class Page {
    public static function byField(): void {
        callable $loader = fn(): int => 1;
        var $page = Core\Task::all({user: $loader, rows: fn(): array<int> => [1]});
        echo Core\Arr::count($page->rows);
    }

    public static function byArgument(): void {
        var $set = {user: fn(): int => 1};
        var $page = Core\Task::all($set);
        echo 1;
    }
}

Page::byField();
Page::byArgument();
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0774]: the field `user` must be written as an `fn` literal
   --> case.nvs:15:43
%A
error[E0773]: this argument must be written out as `{...}` at the call site
   --> case.nvs:21:36
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
